1gq2|n|The son of Saturn and Ops, the god of the waters, especially of the sea. He is represented as bearing a trident for a scepter. ; The remotest known planet of our system, discovered -- as a result of the computations of Leverrier, of Paris -- by Galle, of Berlin, September 23, 1846. Its mean distance from the sun is about 2,775,000,000 miles, and its period of revolution is about 164,78 years.	n:pj8,137,3~pj8,137,3
